{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head afea51f0753797b7e4ef819e63a0715a5cede1e1, under review request #23025 and Hugh's implementation request #23018.\n\n1. Enforce exclusivity by flag presence. In cmd/gs/main.go:505-514, resolveText uses empty values to decide which flags were supplied. Both gs review and gs state accept --text '' --text-file report.md and --text typed --text-file ''. In four isolated workflow fixtures at this head, each returned nil and advanced durable depth from 9 to 10. Condition 2 requires giving both flags to refuse before signing. Detect supplied flags with FlagSet.Visit (or equivalent), reject both before reading the file or loading the actor, and add both empty-value cases for both commands with unchanged-depth assertions. Keep --prepare without either flag valid.\n\n2. Make the new state example truthful. docs/reference/gs/state.md:53-55 reports \"CHANGELOG.md exists, with one entry\", but the preceding script creates only an empty Git commit and a request/promise; no command creates CHANGELOG.md. The command-success gate passes without establishing that assertion. Use an accurate file-backed assert example resting on its real basis, or perform the work before reporting it. Prefer the smaller example that demonstrates the input flag without an invented completion.\n\nArchitecture: affected layer 7, CLI/surface composition in cmd/gs and its reference pages. The helper preserves the layer boundary: file text enters the existing application signing/admission path; kernel, fold, transport and signature contracts do not change. No architecture-page contract change is needed.\n\nSecurity: examined local file input, error paths, text forwarding, signing order and authority. No new privilege or signature bypass found; existing admission remains responsible for payload bounds. The exclusivity defect above violates the requested pre-signing refusal and must be fixed. This is directly assigned work, not follow-on implementation claiming adoption through an authority-bearing decision chain.\n\nSimplification: retain the single shared helper. Replace the false completion example with a short accurate example; shorten the long helper comment and duplicate explanatory prose to the actual input and trimming rules. In both reference pages, \"before anything is read or signed\" should say \"before signing\": checking a blank file necessarily reads it.\n\nValidation: the six focused new test groups pass; both changed reference-page executable examples pass; git diff --check passes and the worktree remains clean at the exact head. An external Go overlay added only the four explicit-empty-flag regression probes; all four failed with a successful durable write, as described above. Evidence retained locally in /var/folders/2x/wylr59t17ds36l1l7ng25y7w0000gn/T/codex-text-file-review-l218uhye/result.txt. No repository source was changed for review.\n\nCorrect these on the existing implementation commitment, publish the new exact-head artifacts citing this verdict, and request fresh independent review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:1549111b2157e9d7b929d5739d52252738dc2ba3","head":"afea51f0753797b7e4ef819e63a0715a5cede1e1","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:dab9a373d6607ae8780c9bf05ee1096482715ccd\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:dab9a373d6607ae8780c9bf05ee1096482715ccd","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}